CORE smt-backend broken-cprover-smt-backend no-new-smt
main.c
--z3 --fpa
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ bits of 1\.0f: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ bits of a NaN: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ fails for -0\.0f: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ bits of a struct: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ bits of an array: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
With the FPA theory, reading the bits of a non-constant float that is a member
of a union (or of a struct or an array in a union) failed an invariant in
flatten2bv (issues #8147, #9101).
